Z||000010||Seanh||01-12-2001||08:39 PM||||I know the family isnt looking into another car right now, but would you really be if your son was in a nearly fatal car crash? I think another Fiero or any year, would still be a good idea. Anyone can give him money, and will trought the family's donation account, but who would be thinking of getting him another Fiero? I think he would like that (If he's into Fieros like we are) more then more money. If not, he can always sell it and take the money, and we would donate the left over money from the car purchase to the family. Just my $0.02<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
